# Design Tokens (Figma JSON)

`DesignTokens/figma/` is the design source of truth. Do not edit it during UI work.

## Never modify

- `DesignTokens/figma/colors.json`
- `DesignTokens/figma/typography.json`
- `DesignTokens/figma/spacing.json`
- `DesignTokens/figma/radius.json`
- `DesignTokens/figma/stroke.json`
- `DesignTokens/figma/splash-colors.json`

Do not change these unless the user explicitly exports updated tokens from Figma and asks to replace them.

## What to do instead

- Use existing assets: `Color.buttonSecondaryWhite`, `Color.foregroundPrimaryWhite`, etc.
- Use `MatchFlow/DesignSystem/`: `DSTextStyle`, `DSSpacing`, `DSRadius`, `DSStroke`
- Fix screens in Swift views (`IntroView`, `LoginView`, etc.), not in JSON

## Examples

```swift
// ✅ GOOD — consume token in UI
Text("Sign up")
    .textStyle(.body1Semibold)
    .background(Color.buttonSecondaryWhite)

// ❌ BAD — patching typography.json to match one screen
// editing DesignTokens/figma/typography.json fontSize from 15 to 17
```

## Adding new tokens

Only when the user provides a new Figma export. Add new files or replace wholesale — never rewrite existing JSON in place during UI iterations.
